        ('Samurai Scout', 'A reconnaissance specialist gathering intelligence on threats to United Cities interests. They patrol borderlands and report on bandit movements and rival faction activities.'),
        ('Samurai Sergeant', 'A field commander leading small samurai units in patrols and engagements. They enforce discipline among troops and execute orders from higher-ranking officers.'),
        ('Sand Ninja', 'A stealthy warrior trained in desert combat and infiltration tactics. They serve their faction through reconnaissance and swift strikes against enemies.'),
        ('Sand Ninja Jounin', 'An elite commander of Sand Ninja forces with years of combat experience. They lead squads on dangerous missions and train lower-ranking operatives.'),
        ('Sanda''s Noble Guard', 'A professional soldier sworn to protect Sanda and her interests. They maintain order and defend against threats with disciplined martial skill.'),
        ('Scavenger', 'A wasteland survivor who picks through ruins and battlefields for salvageable goods. They trade scrap and equipment to make a meager living.'),
        ('Scrawny Cannibal', 'A malnourished member of a cannibal tribe struggling to survive in harsh lands. Desperation has driven them to hunt other humans for sustenance.'),
        ('Screamer Unit', 'A specialized soldier equipped with sonic weaponry designed to disorient enemies. They operate in coordinated groups to maximize their tactical advantage.'),
        ('Shek Adventurer', 'A wandering Shek seeking glory and worthy opponents across the wasteland. They travel between towns taking contracts and testing their strength.'),
        ('Shek Barman', 'A Shek who serves drinks and manages a tavern establishment. They maintain order in their bar with intimidating presence and occasional force.'),
        ('Shek Engineer', 'A technically-minded Shek who maintains equipment and constructs defenses. They apply their strength and intellect to building and repair work.'),
        ('Shek Fighter', 'A combat-trained Shek warrior proficient in melee weapons and brawling. They seek honorable battles and respect strength above all else.'),
        ('Shek Medic', 'A Shek trained in battlefield medicine and emergency treatment. They patch up wounded warriors so they can return to honorable combat.'),
        ('Shek Recruit', 'A young Shek beginning their martial training and warrior education. They perform basic duties while learning combat skills from veterans.'),
        ('Shek Retainer', 'A loyal Shek warrior bound in service to a specific leader or household. They provide personal protection and carry out their master''s orders.'),
        ('Shek Scout', 'A fast-moving Shek who surveys terrain and tracks enemy movements. They report intelligence back to their commanders before battles.'),
        ('Shek Warrior', 'A seasoned Shek combatant hardened by numerous battles and conflicts. They embody their race''s martial culture and hunger for worthy challenges.'),
        ('Shinobi Citizen', 'A civilian resident of Shinobi Thieves territory living under their protection. They pay tribute and follow the faction''s laws in exchange for security.'),
        ('Shinobi Guard', 'An armed enforcer who patrols Shinobi Thieves settlements and territory. They protect faction interests and ensure tribute is properly collected.'),
        ('Shinobi Trader', 'A merchant operating under Shinobi Thieves oversight and protection. They buy and sell goods while paying their share to the faction.'),
        ('Shop Guard', 'A hired security professional who protects a store from thieves and troublemakers. They stand watch during business hours and deter potential criminals.'),
        ('Shrieking Bandit', 'A wild raider known for screaming battle cries during attacks. They terrorize travelers and small settlements for plunder and supplies.'),
        ('Skeleton Adventurer', 'An ancient skeleton exploring the world and seeking purpose in the current age. They wander between settlements offering their ageless experience for hire.'),
        ('Skeleton Bandit', 'A skeleton outlaw who preys on travelers and caravans for profit. Their mechanical body requires no food, only repair materials and equipment.'),
        ('Skeleton Barman', 'A skeleton who operates a drinking establishment serving organic customers. They never tire and have accumulated centuries of bartending knowledge.'),
        ('Skeleton Civilian', 'A skeleton living peacefully among other races in settled areas. They work various trades, unburdened by hunger or aging.'),
        ('Skeleton Doctor', 'A skeleton physician with extensive medical knowledge from past ages. They treat patients with techniques refined over centuries of practice.'),
        ('Skeleton Drifter', 'A wandering skeleton with no fixed home or allegiance, surviving through odd jobs and scavenging. They drift between settlements seeking purpose or simply avoiding trouble.'),
        ('Skeleton Grayflayer', 'An ancient skeleton warrior who has survived countless battles and wars. Their experience makes them formidable combatants despite their weathered frames.'),
        ('Skeleton Recruit', 'A newly activated or recently freed skeleton learning the ways of their current faction. They possess basic combat training but lack the experience of older models.'),
        ('Skeleton Resident', 'A skeleton who has settled permanently in a town or outpost, contributing to the community through labor or trade. They have found stability after potentially centuries of wandering.'),
        ('Skin Bandit', 'A deranged individual obsessed with collecting and wearing the skin of victims. They operate in gangs that hunt travelers across the wastes.'),
        ('Slave', 'A person stripped of freedom and forced into labor through capture or debt. They endure harsh conditions under constant guard and threat of punishment.'),
        ('Slave Escapee', 'Someone who has recently broken free from bondage and now flees their former masters. They carry the scars and trauma of enslavement while seeking a new life.'),
        ('Slave Hunter', 'A tracker specialized in recapturing escaped slaves for bounties. They employ nets, clubs, and tracking skills to return runaways to their owners.'),
        ('Slave Recruits', 'Newly captured individuals being processed into slavery, not yet broken or assigned permanent duties. They represent fresh acquisitions for the slave trade.'),
        ('Slave/Civilian', 'An enslaved person forced to perform domestic or urban labor within settlements. They serve households, shops, or public works under watchful supervision.'),
        ('Slave/Outlaw', 'A criminal sentenced to penal slavery as punishment for their crimes. They work in the harshest conditions as both punishment and deterrent.'),
        ('Slave/Ronin', 'A former warrior or samurai reduced to slavery through defeat or capture. Their combat skills make them valuable but dangerous property.'),
        ('Slave/Tough', 'An enslaved laborer assigned to physically demanding work in mines, farms, or construction. Their strength is exploited until exhaustion or death.'),
        ('Slave/Warrior', 'A slave forced to fight for their master''s entertainment or military purposes. They battle in arenas or serve as expendable troops.'),
        ('Slavemonger', 'A merchant who specializes in buying and selling slaves as commodities. They operate markets and auctions where human lives are traded for profit.'),
        ('Slaver', 'An individual who captures, trades, or guards slaves as their primary occupation. They view people as property and profit from human suffering.'),
        ('Slaver Boss', 'A leader commanding a slaver operation or camp with multiple subordinates. They manage the business of enslavement and extraction of labor.'),
        ('Slaver Caravan Boss', 'The commander of a mobile slaving operation that travels between regions buying and selling captives. They coordinate guards and manage valuable human cargo.'),
        ('Slaver Caravan Guard', 'An armed escort protecting slave caravans from raiders and preventing escape attempts during transport. They maintain order through intimidation and violence.'),
        ('Slaver Guard', 'A watchman stationed at slave camps or markets to prevent escapes and suppress resistance. They enforce discipline through brutality and constant surveillance.'),
        ('Slaver Heavy Guard', 'Elite enforcers equipped with superior armor and weapons to handle dangerous slaves or threats. They serve as the backbone of major slaving operations.'),
        ('Smuggler', 'A trader who moves contraband goods across faction borders, avoiding taxes and legal restrictions. They know secret routes and bribe the right officials.'),
        ('Sniperbot', 'An automated security unit programmed for long-range precision elimination of targets. It maintains watch over restricted zones with lethal accuracy.'),
        ('Soldier Drone', 'A basic military robot following simple combat protocols and orders. It serves as expendable infantry in automated defense forces.'),
        ('Soldierbot', 'An advanced combat automaton designed for frontline warfare and security operations. It executes tactical commands with mechanical efficiency and durability.'),
        ('Soldierbot Guard', 'An automated skeleton warrior programmed to defend a specific location or master. Its combat protocols are ancient but still deadly efficient.'),
        ('Starving Vagrant', 'A desperate wanderer on the edge of starvation, surviving day to day through begging or scavenging. They have nothing left to lose and everything to gain.'),
        ('Stormthrall', 'A warrior enslaved or indoctrinated to serve in the most brutal combat roles. They fight without question, broken by their masters or the wasteland itself.'),
        ('Straw Lieutenant', 'A mid-ranking officer in a local militia or bandit group, commanding small squads. They enforce orders and maintain discipline among the lower ranks.'),
        ('Strayed Paladin', 'A former Holy Nation warrior who abandoned or was exiled from their order. They wander seeking redemption or a new purpose beyond their failed faith.'),
        ('Surgeon', 'A skilled medical practitioner who repairs broken bodies in exchange for cats. Their services are expensive but essential in a world of constant violence.'),
        ('Swamp Ninja Chunin', 'A mid-level operative of the Swamp Ninjas, trained in stealth and assassination. They lead small teams on raids and intelligence gathering missions.'),
        ('Swamp Ninja Genin', 'A junior member of the Swamp Ninjas still learning the arts of infiltration and combat. They handle basic reconnaissance and support roles for the organization.'),
        ('Swamp Ninja Jonin', 'An elite Swamp Ninja commander with mastery over stealth warfare and tactical operations. They plan and execute the most critical missions for their faction.'),
        ('Swamper Bar Thug', 'A rough enforcer who keeps order in swamp town drinking establishments. They settle disputes with fists and blades when customers get too rowdy.'),
        ('Swamper Casino Dealer', 'A card and dice handler in the gambling dens of swamp settlements. They run games with practiced skill while watching for cheaters and troublemakers.'),
        ('Swamper Gate Guard', 'A sentry posted at the entrances to swamp settlements, checking travelers and collecting tolls. They turn away unwanted visitors and sound alarms during attacks.'),
        ('Swamper Non-Gang', 'An ordinary resident of the swamp towns trying to survive outside gang affiliations. They work honest jobs while avoiding the attention of local criminals.'),
        ('Sword For Hire', 'A mercenary warrior who sells their blade to whoever pays the most cats. They have no loyalty beyond the contract and move on when the job is done.'),
        ('Tech Hunter', 'A scavenger and explorer who seeks Ancient technology in ruins across the wasteland. They sell their findings to researchers or keep useful artifacts for themselves.'),
        ('Tech Hunter Adventurer', 'An experienced Tech Hunter who ventures into the most dangerous ruins for rare artifacts. They combine combat skills with knowledge of Ancient sites.'),
        ('Tech Hunter Gate Guard', 'A sentry protecting Tech Hunter outposts and camps from intruders. They screen visitors and defend valuable artifact collections stored within.'),
        ('Tech Hunter Guard', 'A warrior employed to protect Tech Hunter expeditions and facilities. They fight off bandits and creatures while salvage operations are underway.'),
        ('Tech Hunter Recruit', 'A novice member of the Tech Hunters learning to identify and extract Ancient technology. They assist veterans on expeditions while developing survival skills.'),
        ('Tech Hunter Ruins', 'A specialized scavenger operating deep within dangerous Ancient complexes. They navigate deadly security systems and hostile robots to claim lost technology.'),
        ('Tech Hunter Shopkeeper', 'A merchant who buys and sells Ancient artifacts and engineering equipment. They appraise technology and connect scavengers with wealthy collectors.'),
        ('Tenacious Recruit', 'A determined new fighter who refuses to give up despite lacking experience. Their persistence compensates for their current lack of skill and equipment.'),
        ('Territorial Thug', 'A violent enforcer who claims certain areas as their gang''s domain. They shake down travelers and merchants who pass through their controlled territory.'),
        ('Thief', 'A skilled pickpocket and burglar who steals to survive in the harsh world. They operate in shadows, taking what they need from the careless and wealthy.'),
        ('Thief Boss', 'The leader of an organized theft operation controlling multiple pickpockets and burglars. They plan heists and fence stolen goods through underground networks.'),
        ('Thief Fence', 'A shadowy merchant who buys stolen goods without asking questions. They operate from hidden locations and pay a fraction of market value for hot merchandise.'),
        ('Thrall', 'A broken slave who has endured years of brutal servitude in the Holy Nation. They perform backbreaking labor in fields and mines with little hope of freedom.'),
        ('Trade Goods Shopkeeper', 'A merchant specializing in raw materials and crafting supplies for travelers and craftsmen. They stock everything from iron plates to fabrics at fair prices.'),
        ('Traders Guard', 'A hired sword protecting merchant caravans as they cross dangerous territories. They must stay alert for bandits, beasts, and worse on the long roads.'),
        ('Traitorous Bar Thug', 'A disloyal enforcer willing to sell out their own gang for the right price. They lurk in taverns waiting for opportunities to betray their companions.'),
        ('Twitchy Bar Thug', 'A paranoid criminal whose nerves are shot from too many close calls and bad dust. They start fights over imagined slights and can barely hold a drink steady.'),
        ('UC Armour Trader', 'An official merchant licensed by the United Cities to sell protective gear. They offer quality armor at premium prices within UC territories.'),
        ('UC Citizen', 'A law-abiding resident of the United Cities who pays their taxes and follows the rules. They work honest jobs and avoid trouble with the Samurai enforcers.'),
        ('UC Hat Vendor', 'A specialized trader dealing exclusively in headwear from practical helmets to decorative hats. They maintain a small stall in UC marketplaces.'),
        ('UC Weapon Trader', 'A licensed arms dealer operating under United Cities authority. They sell quality blades and weapons to those who can afford the steep prices.'),
        ('Ugly Bar Thug', 'A scarred and brutish criminal whose appearance alone intimidates most patrons. They enforce protection rackets and collect debts through violence.'),
        ('Undertaker', 'A grim professional who handles corpse disposal in towns and cities. They collect bodies from the streets and prepare them for whatever burial customs apply.'),
        ('Unfortunate Recruit', 'A desperate soul who joined a faction out of necessity rather than conviction. They lack training and experience, making them cannon fodder in conflicts.'),
        ('Unique Recruits', 'Exceptional individuals with distinctive skills or backgrounds waiting to be discovered. Each has their own story and reason for joining a wandering group.'),
        ('United Hero', 'A celebrated warrior who has earned fame fighting for the United Cities. They command respect and higher pay for their proven combat abilities.'),
        ('Upgraded Skeleton Bandit', 'An ancient machine outlaw enhanced with superior components and weapons. They prey on travelers with mechanical efficiency and no mercy.'),
        ('Upgraded Skeleton Guard', 'A mechanical sentinel fitted with advanced armor plating and combat protocols. They protect important locations with tireless vigilance.'),
        ('Upgraded Watchbot', 'An enhanced security automaton patrolling settlements with improved sensors. They detect criminals and intruders more effectively than standard models.'),
        ('Vigilante Chief', 'A self-appointed leader of citizens who enforce their own justice outside the law. They organize patrols and punishments against those they deem criminals.'),
        ('Wall Man', 'A guard stationed on settlement walls watching for approaching threats. They spend long shifts scanning the horizon for bandits, beasts, or hostile forces.'),
        ('Wandering Assassin', 'A professional killer who travels between cities seeking contracts. They work for anyone who can meet their price, no questions asked.'),
        ('Waystation Barman', 'A tavern keeper running a remote establishment along major trade routes. They serve drinks and food to weary travelers while hearing all the latest rumors.'),
        ('Weak Thrall', 'A newly enslaved person not yet broken by the brutality of servitude. They still possess some spirit but lack the strength to resist their masters.'),
        ('White Eyebrow Grunt', 'A low-ranking member of the White Eyebrow bandit gang. They follow orders and participate in raids across the northern territories.'),
        ('Yabuta Outlaw', 'A criminal operating in the Yabuta region, preying on isolated farms and travelers. They survive through theft and violence in the harsh borderlands.')
), normalized AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT TRIM(name) AS name, TRIM(description) AS description
    FROM source_rows
    WHERE TRIM(name) <> '' AND TRIM(description) <> ''
)
DELETE FROM bio_random
WHERE LOWER(type) = 'occupation'
  AND LOWER(COALESCE(name, '')) IN (SELECT LOWER(name) FROM normalized);

WITH source_rows(name, description) AS (
    VALUES
        ('Adventurer Recruit', 'A novice wanderer seeking fortune and purpose in the harsh wastelands. They possess minimal combat training but boundless optimism that reality will soon temper.'),
        ('Alpha Gurgler', 'The dominant member of a Gurgler pack, leading through savage strength and territorial aggression. This creature commands lesser Gurglers in their hunting grounds with brutal efficiency.'),
        ('Anti-Slaver', 'A freedom fighter dedicated to dismantling the slave trade through direct action and violence. They patrol routes and raid slaver camps to liberate the imprisoned.'),
        ('Anti-Slaver Jonin', 'An experienced commander within the anti-slavery movement who leads strike teams against slaver operations. Their tactical expertise has freed hundreds from bondage across multiple regions.'),
        ('Armour King''s Thrall', 'A slave forced to serve in the Armour King''s domain, laboring under constant threat of violence. They perform menial tasks and manufacturing work to sustain their master''s operations.'),
        ('Armoury Droneguard', 'A security automaton assigned to protect weapon stockpiles and manufacturing facilities. This skeleton guard follows ancient protocols without question or mercy.'),
        ('Band of Bones', 'A wandering skeleton who has rejected their ancient purpose to roam freely. They survive through scavenging and occasional mercenary work in the borderlands.'),
        ('Bar Fisherman', 'A patron who spends their days drinking away earnings from selling their meager catches. The bar has become more familiar than the docks they once frequented.'),
        ('Bar Thug Drunk', 'A violent troublemaker who haunts taverns looking for fights and easy marks. Alcohol fuels their aggression and poor decision-making in equal measure.'),
        ('Bar fly', 'A perpetual tavern dweller who survives on gossip, cheap alcohol, and occasional odd jobs. They know everyone''s business but rarely leave their favorite stool.'),
        ('Berserker', 'A warrior who channels rage into devastating combat prowess, abandoning defense for pure aggression. They live for battle and care nothing for their own safety.'),
        ('Black Dog Bodyguard', 'A hired enforcer working for the Black Dog gang, protecting their interests through intimidation and violence. They ensure debts are paid and rivals stay clear of gang territory.'),
        ('Black Dragon Genin', 'A low-ranking ninja operative within the Black Dragon Ninjas organization. They perform reconnaissance, theft, and assassination contracts for their shadowy masters.'),
        ('Blackshifter', 'A member of the Blackshifters faction operating in the dangerous Venge region. They scavenge ancient technology and defend their territory from both wildlife and rival groups.'),
        ('Blood Raider', 'A savage marauder who attacks travelers and settlements for plunder and sport. They mark their armor with the blood of victims as trophies of conquest.'),
        ('Bookshop Trader', 'A merchant specializing in rare texts, maps, and technical blueprints salvaged from ruins. They cater to scholars, engineers, and those seeking forgotten knowledge.'),
        ('Boot Trader', 'A vendor dealing exclusively in footwear for the wasteland traveler. They understand that proper boots mean the difference between survival and becoming buzzard food.'),
        ('Bounty Hunter', 'A professional tracker who captures or kills marked targets for payment. They work independently, following contracts from various factions and settlements.'),
        ('Broken Model 30', 'A malfunctioning skeleton unit from an ancient production line, operating with damaged programming. Their erratic behavior makes them unpredictable and often hostile to organics.'),
        ('Broken Skeleton', 'A damaged automaton whose original purpose has been lost to time and malfunction. They wander aimlessly, sometimes aggressive, sometimes simply confused by their deteriorated state.'),
        ('Broken Skeleton Bandit', 'A rogue skeleton who has turned to banditry after their systems degraded beyond proper function. They attack travelers with corrupted logic driving their violent behavior.'),
        ('Cannibal', 'A member of the tribal cannibal groups that hunt humans for food in the northern regions. They view outsiders as nothing more than meat to sustain their communities.'),
        ('Cannibal Chief', 'The leader of a cannibal tribe who commands hunting parties and territorial defense. Their authority is maintained through strength and successful provision of flesh for their people.'),
        ('Cannibal Hunter', 'A hardened anti-cannibal warrior from the Cannibal Hunters faction, trained to track raiding tribes and rescue captives. They patrol northern frontiers in squads, using practical weapons and disciplined coordination.'),
        ('Cannibal Hunter Captain', 'An experienced commander of Cannibal Hunter patrols with a record of successful anti-cannibal operations. They coordinate ambushes, assign scouts, and direct their hunters to protect settlements and travelers.'),
        ('Caravan Drone', 'A pack animal or laborer bound to a trading caravan, carrying goods across dangerous wastelands. They haul supplies without complaint through dust storms and bandit territory.'),
        ('Caravan Guard', 'A hired mercenary protecting merchant caravans from bandits and wildlife. They patrol the caravan''s flanks with weapons ready, expecting ambush at any moment.'),
        ('Caravan Trader Boss', 'The merchant leader of a trading caravan who negotiates deals and manages routes. They risk their capital on dangerous roads in pursuit of profit.'),
        ('Citizen', 'An ordinary resident of one of Kenshi''s settlements, working to survive another day. They pay taxes, avoid trouble, and hope the walls keep the dangers out.'),
        ('City Hero', 'A renowned warrior who has defended their settlement from major threats. Their past deeds earn them respect and free drinks in local bars.'),
        ('Cloud Ninja', 'A member of the secretive Cloud Ninja faction operating in the northern regions. They strike from shadows and demand tribute from those crossing their territory.'),
        ('Clunknad Spanner', 'A mechanic specializing in skeleton repair and maintenance work. They keep the ancient mechanical beings functional with salvaged parts and technical expertise.'),
        ('Cook Recruit', 'A novice cook learning to prepare meals in a bar or settlement kitchen. They turn whatever ingredients are available into something barely edible.'),
        ('Crab Barman', 'A crab person tending bar in a settlement tavern. They serve grog and listen to travelers'' stories while keeping their establishment orderly.'),
        ('Crab Man', 'A crustacean humanoid native to Kenshi''s coastal and swamp regions. They live in their own communities with distinct culture and physiology.'),
        ('Crab Patron', 'A crab person customer drinking at a bar or visiting a shop. They spend their hard-earned cats on supplies and entertainment like anyone else.'),
        ('Crab Raider', 'A hostile crab warrior who attacks travelers and settlements for loot. They use their natural armor and strength to overwhelm victims.'),
        ('Crab Raider Civilian', 'A non-combatant member of a crab raider community. They maintain camps and support the warriors between raids.'),
        ('Crabsmith', 'A crab artisan who crafts weapons and armor in their workshop. Their strong claws allow them to work metal with unique techniques.'),
        ('Crazy Bar Thug', 'An unhinged troublemaker who starts fights in taverns without provocation. Their unpredictable violence makes them dangerous to everyone nearby.'),
        ('Crow Face', 'A member of the Crow Face bandit group that preys on weak travelers. They wear distinctive masks while robbing anyone unable to defend themselves.'),
        ('Deadcat Fisherman', 'A fisherman working the waters near Deadcat territory in the swamps. They harvest what the murky waters provide to sell at market.'),
        ('Deadcat Vendor', 'A merchant operating in Deadcat settlements selling goods to locals and visitors. They trade in fish, supplies, and whatever else moves through the swamps.'),
        ('Doctor', 'A medical practitioner who treats wounds and illnesses with whatever supplies are available. They patch up fighters and workers so they can survive another day.'),
        ('Drifter', 'A wanderer moving between settlements with no permanent home or allegiance. They take odd jobs and keep moving to stay ahead of trouble.'),
        ('Drone', 'A worker performing menial labor in a settlement or faction. They haul materials, farm crops, and do whatever tasks their masters assign.'),
        ('Droneguard', 'A low-ranking soldier assigned to guard duty at gates or patrols. They watch for threats while more elite warriors handle serious combat.'),
        ('Drunken Bar Thug', 'An intoxicated brawler looking for any excuse to throw punches in a tavern. Alcohol fuels their aggression and clouds their judgment completely.'),
        ('Dust Bandit', 'A common desert raider who survives by robbing weak travelers and caravans. They operate in gangs across the arid wastelands, taking what they need by force.'),
        ('Dust Bandit Bowman', 'A ranged specialist among the Dust Bandits who provides covering fire during raids. They weaken targets from distance before their allies close in for melee.'),
        ('Dust Boss', 'A hardened leader who commands scavenger gangs in the wasteland''s most desolate regions. They maintain control through ruthless enforcement and knowledge of survival in dust-choked territories.'),
        ('Elite Droneguard', 'A highly trained soldier serving in the most disciplined military units. They execute orders with mechanical precision and are equipped with superior armor and weapons.'),
        ('Elite Hunter', 'A seasoned tracker who specializes in hunting dangerous beasts and high-value bounties. Their skills command premium rates from those who can afford the best.'),
        ('Empire Adventurer', 'A wanderer from the United Cities seeking fortune and glory across the continent. They balance imperial upbringing with the practical needs of survival in lawless lands.'),
        ('Empire Mercenary', 'A professional soldier who sells their combat skills to United Cities nobles and merchants. They maintain a veneer of civilization while performing brutal work for coin.'),
        ('Empire Peasant', 'A common laborer struggling to survive under the United Cities'' strict social hierarchy. They work fields, haul goods, and pay taxes while dreaming of a better life.'),
        ('Empire Recruit', 'A newly enlisted soldier in the United Cities military forces. They are still learning discipline and combat while adjusting to the harsh realities of service.'),
        ('Engineer Recruit', 'An apprentice learning the technical skills of machinery repair and construction. They assist experienced engineers while developing expertise in maintaining equipment and structures.'),
        ('Error Code 0xFFFFFF', 'A malfunctioning skeleton whose corrupted programming has left them in an unstable state. Their behavior is unpredictable and their original purpose lost to system failures.'),
        ('ErrorCode 0x000000', 'A skeleton suffering from critical system errors that have damaged their core functions. They struggle with basic tasks as corrupted data interferes with their operations.'),
        ('Escaped Servant', 'A former domestic worker who fled their master''s household to seek freedom. They possess useful skills but live in constant fear of recapture and punishment.'),
        ('Escaped Slave', 'A fugitive who broke free from bondage and now runs from slave hunters. Every day of freedom is a victory, but they must remain vigilant to avoid recapture.'),
        ('Ex-Servant', 'A freed domestic worker who once served in a noble household. They carry skills in cooking, cleaning, and etiquette but must now forge an independent path.'),
        ('Farmer', 'A agricultural worker who cultivates crops in one of the continent''s harsh environments. They understand irrigation, soil quality, and the constant struggle against famine.'),
        ('Farmer Recruit', 'A field hand with no combat experience seeking a different life. They bring strong backs and determination but lack any martial training.'),
        ('Fighter Recruit', 'An untested warrior beginning their journey in combat training. They possess raw potential but need experience before becoming effective in battle.'),
        ('Fish and Drugs Seller', 'A merchant dealing in both seafood and hashish from a market stall. They navigate the legal gray areas of trade while serving customers with varied needs.'),
        ('Flotsam Jonin', 'A high-ranking member of the Flotsam Ninjas who has proven their worth through successful operations. They lead missions and train lower-ranked members in the ways of their organization.'),
        ('Flotsam Ninja', 'A member of the Flotsam Ninjas, operating in the shadows for their organization''s goals. They specialize in stealth, infiltration, and covert operations across the continent.'),
        ('Flotsam Recruit', 'A new initiate into the Flotsam Ninjas still learning the basics of stealth and combat. They perform simple tasks while proving their loyalty and capability to the organization.'),
        ('Flotsam Refugee', 'A displaced person who sought shelter with the Flotsam Ninjas after losing everything. They work odd jobs for the organization while hoping to earn full membership.'),
        ('Fog Heavy', 'A powerful warrior serving the Fogmen tribes in the deadly fog zones. They are stronger and more dangerous than common Fogmen, often leading hunting parties.'),
        ('Fogman', 'A pale, primitive humanoid dwelling in the fog-shrouded regions of the continent. They hunt in packs and drag victims back to their nests for dark purposes.'),
        ('Garret''s slave', 'A person held in bondage by the slaver named Garret. They endure harsh conditions while serving their master''s demands in his operation.'),
        ('Generic Recruits', 'Wanderers and drifters available for hire with no special background or skills. They represent the desperate and hopeful seeking purpose and coin through employment.'),
        ('Goat Herder', 'Tends to herds of goats in the arid wastes, providing meat and hides to settlements. Spends days wandering dusty plains keeping the animals safe from predators and bandits.'),
        ('Goat Man', 'A wild hermit who has abandoned civilization to live among goats in remote regions. Speaks rarely and trusts animals more than people.'),
        ('Gorillo Bandit', 'A brutish raider who preys on travelers through mountain passes and rocky terrain. Uses overwhelming strength and crude weapons to intimidate victims into surrender.'),
        ('Grass Pirate', 'A bandit who ambushes caravans traveling through the tall grasslands of the border zones. Relies on the concealment of vegetation to launch surprise attacks.'),
        ('Grayflayer', 'A skilled skinner who processes animal hides and leathers for trade. Works with tough gray-skinned beasts that roam the wastes.'),
        ('Guild Plastic Surgeon', 'A medical specialist who repairs disfigurements and injuries for paying customers in guild-controlled towns. Operates a clinic where the wealthy can restore their appearance.'),
        ('Gunner Recruit', 'A novice crossbow operator undergoing basic training in ranged combat. Still learning proper aim and reload techniques under experienced gunners.'),
        ('Gurgler', 'A wretched cannibal dwelling in the Fog Islands who hunts lost travelers. Emits disturbing sounds while stalking prey through the mist.'),
        ('Hero Boss', 'A legendary warrior who leads a powerful faction through reputation and combat prowess. Commands absolute loyalty from followers through demonstrated strength.'),
        ('High Overseer', 'A senior administrator who manages slave operations and labor camps for the Holy Nation. Enforces quotas and punishes inefficiency with brutal discipline.'),
        ('High Paladin', 'An elite warrior-priest of the Holy Nation who enforces religious law with sword and scripture. Commands respect through both martial skill and spiritual authority.'),
        ('Hive Bandit', 'A hiveless outcast who turned to raiding after exile from the collective. Operates in small groups with other desperate exiles.'),
        ('Hive Bandit Leader', 'Commands a gang of hiveless criminals who prey on traders and settlements. Maintains order through pheromone authority and tactical cunning.'),
        ('Hive Caravan Boss', 'Organizes and protects trade expeditions between hive villages and foreign settlements. Coordinates multiple workers to transport goods safely across dangerous territories.'),
        ('Hive Trader', 'A merchant from the Western Hive who exchanges goods with outsiders at village markets. Offers unique hive-produced items and foodstuffs.'),
        ('Hiveless Farmer', 'An exiled hive worker who now cultivates crops independently in the borderlands. Struggles with isolation after losing the comfort of the collective.'),
        ('Hiveless Fighter', 'A hive exile who survives through mercenary work and combat skills. Wanders without the guidance of queen pheromones.'),
        ('Hiveless Gunner', 'A hive outcast trained in crossbow combat who sells their marksmanship to whoever pays. Lives a solitary existence far from any hive village.'),
        ('Hiveless Recruit', 'A recently exiled hive member seeking purpose by joining a military organization. Still adjusting to life without the collective''s mental connection.'),
        ('Holy Armour Trader', 'Sells plate armor and chainmail approved by the Holy Nation''s religious standards. Operates a shop in Phoenix or other holy cities.'),
        ('Holy Barman', 'Serves food and drink in a Holy Nation tavern while ensuring no sinful behavior occurs. Reports violations of religious law to local paladins.'),
        ('Holy Boot Trader', 'Specializes in selling footwear that meets Holy Nation modesty requirements. Maintains a small shop in prayer-sanctioned settlements.'),
        ('Holy Chosen', 'An elite servant of the Phoenix selected for special missions and religious duties. Represents the highest mortal authority in the Holy Nation.'),
        ('Holy Citizen', 'A loyal follower of Okran living under Holy Nation rule and religious law. Works an honest trade while observing daily prayers and tithes.'),
        ('Holy Citizen/Female', 'A human woman living in Holy Nation territory under strict religious restrictions. Forbidden from combat, leadership, or traveling without male supervision.'),
        ('Holy Citizen/Male', 'A devout follower of Okran who lives within Holy Nation territory and adheres strictly to their religious laws. He works an honest trade or craft while maintaining proper prayer schedules and tithing to the Phoenix.'),
        ('Holy Construction Trader', 'A merchant authorized by the Holy Nation to sell building materials and construction supplies to faithful citizens. He ensures all transactions follow Okran''s law and refuses service to skeletons and unbelievers.'),
        ('Holy Farm Leader', 'An experienced farmer who oversees agricultural operations on Holy Nation lands and manages other workers. He ensures crops are properly tithed to the church while maintaining productivity through Okran''s blessed labor.'),
        ('Holy Farmer', 'A humble agricultural worker who toils in the fields to feed the Holy Nation''s faithful population. He believes honest farm work is sacred duty under Okran''s watchful eye.'),
        ('Holy Farmer Wife', 'A woman bound by Holy Nation law to support her husband''s farming efforts through domestic labor and field assistance. She lives a restricted life of service, forbidden from combat or independent travel.'),
        ('Holy Nation Engineer', 'A skilled technician who maintains equipment and structures while adhering to the Phoenix''s restrictions on forbidden technology. He works within religious guidelines to keep settlements functional without violating Okran''s laws.'),
        ('Holy Nation Female Adventurer', 'A rare woman who has somehow escaped the strict gender restrictions of Holy Nation society to pursue a wanderer''s life. She faces constant danger from both her former people and those who would exploit her fugitive status.'),
        ('Holy Nation Female Recruit', 'A woman who has joined a fighting force outside Holy Nation control, fleeing their oppressive laws. She trains in combat skills that would have been forbidden to her in her homeland.'),
        ('Holy Nation Fighter', 'A warrior devoted to defending the Holy Nation''s borders and enforcing Okran''s will through martial strength. He patrols territories hunting down skeletons, darkened ones, and narko smugglers.'),
        ('Holy Nation Male Adventurer', 'A man who has left the structured life of the Holy Nation to seek fortune and purpose in the wasteland. He carries his faith with him but operates beyond the Phoenix''s direct authority.'),
        ('Holy Nation Male Recruit', 'A young man training to serve the Holy Nation''s military forces as a soldier of Okran. He learns combat techniques and religious doctrine to become a proper defender of the faith.'),
        ('Holy Nation Medic', 'A healer who tends to the wounded faithful using medical knowledge approved by the church. He prays over his patients while binding wounds, believing Okran guides his hands.'),
        ('Holy Nation Robot', 'A skeleton who has somehow gained protection or servitude status within Holy Nation territory, an extremely rare and precarious position. It likely serves under constant supervision and threat, tolerated only for essential technical functions.'),
        ('Holy Priest', 'A ordained minister of Okran who leads prayers, performs rituals, and guides the faithful in proper worship. He holds significant authority in Holy Nation settlements and judges others by strict religious standards.'),
        ('Holy Sentinel', 'An elite warrior-monk dedicated to protecting Holy Nation cities and hunting down enemies of the faith. He has proven his devotion through years of service and combat against the unholy.'),
        ('Holy Servant', 'A laborer assigned to menial tasks in service of the church or Holy Nation officials. He performs cleaning, carrying, and basic maintenance work as an act of humble devotion.'),
        ('Holy Shop Guard', 'A armed watchman stationed at a merchant''s establishment to protect goods and enforce proper conduct. He ensures no forbidden individuals enter and that all customers show proper respect to Okran.'),
        ('Holy Weapon Trader', 'A merchant licensed to sell arms and armor to faithful warriors of the Holy Nation. He refuses service to women, skeletons, and other undesirables while offering blessed weapons to righteous fighters.'),
        ('Hooded Empire Noble Guard', 'An elite soldier assigned to protect United Cities nobility, wearing distinctive concealing garments. He is well-paid and well-equipped to ensure his charge''s safety from assassins and kidnappers.'),
        ('Hound Skeleton', 'An ancient skeleton warrior who serves with the Skeleton Bandits or similar groups, often acting as muscle. It has survived centuries and uses that experience to hunt and fight effectively.'),
        ('Human Mercenary', 'A professional fighter who sells their combat skills to whoever can pay their fee. They wander between contracts, loyal only to cats and their own survival.'),
        ('Hundred Guardian', 'A elite soldier serving the United Cities'' Traders Guild as enforceable muscle and protection. They maintain order in cities and ensure economic interests are defended with lethal efficiency.'),
        ('Hungry Bandit', 'A desperate outlaw driven to robbery by starvation and poverty in the harsh wasteland. They attack travelers with crude weapons, seeking food and supplies rather than wealth.'),
        ('Hungry Bandit Leader', 'A veteran criminal who commands a group of starving outlaws through cunning and ruthlessness. They coordinate ambushes on trade routes, trying to keep their gang fed in the unforgiving wastes.'),
        ('Hydraulic Knight', 'A skeleton warrior equipped with ancient hydraulic-powered armor and weapons from the old empire. They are formidable combatants whose mechanical enhancements make them deadly in battle.'),
        ('Inquisitor', 'A Holy Nation enforcer who roots out heretics and impurity with zealous conviction. They wield authority to interrogate, judge, and execute those who defy Okran''s will.'),
        ('Jonin Elite', 'A master shinobi trained in the deadly arts of assassination and infiltration. They serve as elite operatives for those who can afford their lethal expertise.'),
        ('Karate Drifter', 'A wandering martial artist who has forsaken material possessions for physical perfection. They travel the wastes testing their skills against any worthy opponent.'),
        ('Kral''s Chosen', 'A handpicked warrior sworn to serve Kral directly in the Southern Hive. They represent the finest soldiers the Hive can produce, utterly loyal to their leader.'),
        ('Lagoon Barman', 'A tavern keeper operating in one of the swamp settlements near the coasts. They serve grog and information to smugglers, fishmen, and desperate travelers alike.'),
        ('Legion', 'A soldier serving in the United Cities'' military forces, maintaining order through strength. They patrol territories and enforce the will of the Traders Guild and nobility.'),
        ('Legion Scout', 'A reconnaissance specialist for the United Cities military, ranging ahead of main forces. They gather intelligence on threats from bandits, beasts, and rival factions.'),
        ('Legion Thrall', 'An enslaved warrior forced to fight for the United Cities military. They wear shackles even in battle, their freedom traded for their combat skills.'),
        ('Lost Drone', 'A Hive Worker separated from their Queen and collective purpose. They wander aimlessly, struggling to find meaning without the mental connection that once defined them.'),
        ('Lost Hiver', 'A former Hive member cast out or separated from their colony. They now navigate a confusing world of individualism they were never meant to understand.'),
        ('Lost Prince', 'A displaced noble heir who has fallen from grace and lost their inheritance. They wander the wastes clinging to faded dignity and dreams of restoration.'),
        ('Lower Servant', 'A menial laborer in the service of United Cities nobility or wealthy merchants. They perform degrading tasks for meager pay, always one step above slavery.'),
        ('Machinist', 'A skilled engineer who maintains and repairs the ancient technology scattered across the wastes. They understand skeleton smithing, crossbow mechanisms, and automated defenses.'),
        ('Manhunter', 'A bounty hunter specializing in capturing escaped slaves and wanted criminals. They operate legally within United Cities territory, profiting from others'' desperation.'),
        ('Medic Recruit', 'A novice field surgeon learning to treat wounds in the harsh conditions of the wastes. They carry basic supplies and struggle to save lives with limited resources.'),
        ('Mercenary', 'A professional fighter who sells their blade to the highest bidder. They take contracts ranging from caravan protection to bandit elimination without moral consideration.'),
        ('Mercenary Captain', 'A veteran sellsword who commands a small company of hired fighters. They negotiate contracts and lead their troops through dangerous assignments across the continent.'),
        ('Mercenary Heavy', 'A heavily armored fighter-for-hire specializing in frontline combat. They wear the best equipment their earnings can buy and break enemy formations for paying clients.'),
        ('Moon Guardian', 'A warrior sworn to protect the Stone Golem and its sacred territory. They defend against intruders with fanatical devotion to their ancient charge.'),
        ('Mourn Barman', 'A tavern keeper in the dark, dangerous settlements of Mourn. They serve drinks to cannibals, outcasts, and those with nowhere else to go.'),
        ('Ninja', 'A shadow warrior trained in stealth, assassination, and espionage. They operate from hidden villages, taking contracts that require discretion and lethality.'),
        ('Ninja Guard', 'A shinobi assigned to protect important locations or individuals within ninja territories. They blend sentinel duty with their training in silent killing.'),
        ('Noble Captain', 'A high-ranking military officer from the United Cities aristocracy. They command troops with authority derived from birthright rather than battlefield merit.'),
        ('Noble Hunter', 'An aristocrat who pursues dangerous game and rare beasts as sport. They treat hunting as a display of status, employing servants to handle the actual danger.'),
        ('Nomad', 'A wanderer who survives by traveling between settlements and living off the harsh land. They carry their life on their back, beholden to no faction or master.'),
        ('Nomad Animal Trader', 'Travels between settlements buying and selling pack beasts and other animals. Knows the desert routes well enough to keep their herd alive during long journeys.'),
        ('Old Empire Police Captain', 'Commands a garrison in the crumbling remains of ancient authority. Maintains order through force in territories where the old laws still hold some meaning.'),
        ('Outlaw Adventurer', 'Explores ruins and dangerous territories while dodging bounty hunters. Lives by scavenging ancient tech and selling information about remote locations.'),
        ('Outlaw Cook', 'Prepares meals for a bandit camp or outlaw settlement using whatever ingredients are available. Often works with stolen or scavenged food supplies.'),
        ('Outlaw Farmer', 'Tends illegal crops in hidden locations away from taxing authorities. Grows food to sustain bandit groups or fugitive communities.'),
        ('Outlaw Heavy', 'Heavily armored enforcer for criminal organizations. Specializes in intimidation and frontline combat during raids.'),
        ('Outlaw Medic', 'Patches up wounded criminals and fugitives who cannot seek legitimate medical help. Operates with limited supplies in makeshift clinics.'),
        ('Outlaw Recruit', 'New member of a bandit group or criminal organization learning the trade. Handles basic tasks while training in combat and survival.'),
        ('Outlaw Swordsman', 'Skilled blade fighter working outside the law for bandit crews or mercenary work. Relies on speed and technique in close combat.'),
        ('Outlaw Swordsman Captain', 'Leads a squad of blade-wielding criminals in raids and territorial disputes. Commands through proven skill and ruthless decision-making.'),
        ('Outpost Guard', 'Defends a remote settlement or waystation from raiders and wildlife. Stands watch during long shifts in isolated and dangerous locations.'),
        ('Paladin', 'Holy warrior serving the Holy Nation with unwavering faith. Enforces religious law and hunts those deemed impure or heretical.'),
        ('Paladin Guardian', 'Elite protector assigned to defend Holy Nation temples and high priests. Trained extensively in combat and religious doctrine.'),
        ('Peasant', 'Common laborer struggling to survive under the rule of various factions. Performs whatever work is available to earn enough food to live.'),
        ('Peasant Farmer', 'Works the fields for a landowner or settlement, keeping little of the harvest. Lives season to season hoping for enough yield to pay taxes and eat.'),
        ('Plastic Surgeon', 'Operates a clinic offering facial reconstruction and identity changes. Serves those seeking to escape their past or remove identifying scars.'),
        ('Police', 'Enforces local laws and collects taxes for whatever faction controls the area. Patrols streets looking for criminals and unauthorized activities.'),
        ('Police Chief', 'Commands the law enforcement for a major settlement or district. Answers directly to the ruling faction while managing officers and investigations.'),
        ('Police Sergeant', 'Supervises a squad of officers on patrol and during enforcement actions. Handles day-to-day operations and reports to higher command.'),
        ('Prince', 'Heir or noble of the United Cities ruling class living in luxury. Wields political power while others handle the actual work of governance.'),
        ('Prisoner', 'Captive held in a cage or labor camp awaiting ransom, slavery, or execution. Survives on minimal rations while hoping for escape or release.'),
        ('Reaver Blooded', 'Proven warrior of the Reaver faction who has survived multiple battles. Earns respect through demonstrated violence and loyalty to the tribe.'),
        ('Reaver Ironclad', 'Heavily armored elite fighter among the Reavers wearing the best salvaged equipment. Serves as shock trooper in the most dangerous raids.'),
        ('Reaver Neophyte', 'New initiate to the Reaver tribe undergoing trials to prove their worth. Must demonstrate strength and brutality to earn full membership.'),
        ('Reaver Slave', 'Captive forced to labor for the Reaver tribe under threat of violence. Performs menial tasks and suffers harsh treatment from their captors.'),
        ('Reaver Whelp', 'A young initiate among the cannibalistic Reavers, still learning the brutal ways of their tribe. They perform menial tasks and scavenge battlefields for meat and salvage.'),
        ('Rebel Captain', 'A seasoned leader commanding rebel forces against oppressive factions across the wastes. They coordinate strikes and maintain morale among freedom fighters.'),
        ('Rebel Fighter', 'A common soldier in various resistance movements fighting against tyrannical rule. They engage in guerrilla warfare and defend liberated territories.'),
        ('Rebel Swordsman', 'A blade-wielding insurgent trained in close combat against armored enemies. They specialize in hit-and-run tactics using traditional melee weapons.'),
        ('Rebel Swordsman Veteran', 'A battle-hardened rebel who has survived countless engagements against superior forces. Their expertise with blades makes them invaluable in training new recruits.'),
        ('Rebirth Slave', 'A prisoner forced into backbreaking labor at the Holy Nation''s Rebirth camp. They endure constant punishment while mining and hauling materials under brutal conditions.'),
        ('Recruit', 'A newly enlisted member of a military or mercenary organization with minimal training. They perform basic duties while learning combat skills and discipline.'),
        ('Red Sabre', 'A member of the notorious Red Sabres bandit gang that preys on travelers and settlements. They raid caravans and demand protection money from vulnerable communities.'),
        ('Ronin Armour Trader', 'A wandering merchant specializing in protective gear and armor plates. They travel between settlements offering quality defensive equipment to warriors and adventurers.'),
        ('Ronin Construction Trader', 'An independent vendor dealing in building materials and engineering supplies. They provide essential resources for settlement construction and fortification projects.'),
        ('Ronin Crossbow Trader', 'A traveling arms dealer focused on ranged weaponry and ammunition. They supply crossbows and bolts to those seeking reliable distance combat options.'),
        ('Ronin Hat Trader', 'A merchant offering various headgear from practical helmets to cultural accessories. They cater to both protective needs and personal style preferences.'),
        ('Ronin Weapon Trader', 'An itinerant weapons merchant carrying diverse melee armaments for sale. They offer everything from basic blades to masterwork combat instruments.'),
        ('Royal Soldier Drone', 'A Skeleton warrior serving the Southern Hive Queen with unwavering loyalty. They patrol hive territories and defend against intruders with mechanical precision.'),
        ('Samurai', 'A professional warrior serving the United Cities nobility with discipline and martial skill. They enforce laws, collect taxes, and maintain order in UC territories.'),
        ('Samurai Captain', 'A high-ranking officer commanding samurai units and overseeing regional security operations. They answer directly to nobles and coordinate military responses to threats.'),
        ('Samurai Conscript', 'A recently drafted soldier serving mandatory military service in United Cities forces. They receive basic training while performing garrison and patrol duties.'),
        ('Samurai Elite', 'A masterfully trained warrior representing the finest of United Cities military tradition. They serve as bodyguards to nobility and lead critical combat operations.'),
        ('Samurai Gate Guard', 'A sentinel posted at city entrances to inspect travelers and enforce entry regulations. They check for contraband and collect gate fees from visitors.'),
        ('Samurai Gate Sergeant', 'A veteran guard supervising gate security operations and managing subordinate sentries. They make judgment calls on suspicious individuals and coordinate with city authorities.'),
        ('Samurai Heavy', 'A heavily armored warrior trained to hold defensive positions and break enemy lines. They wear the thickest plates and wield devastating weapons in prolonged combat.'),
        ('Samurai Police', 'An urban enforcer maintaining law and order within United Cities settlements. They patrol streets, investigate crimes, and arrest those who violate city ordinances.'),
        ('Samurai Rogue', 'A former samurai who abandoned their post or was dishonorably discharged from service. They wander as masterless warriors, selling their skills to survive.'),
        ('Samurai Scout', 'A reconnaissance specialist gathering intelligence on threats to United Cities interests. They patrol borderlands and report on bandit movements and rival faction activities.'),
        ('Samurai Sergeant', 'A field commander leading small samurai units in patrols and engagements. They enforce discipline among troops and execute orders from higher-ranking officers.'),
        ('Sand Ninja', 'A stealthy warrior trained in desert combat and infiltration tactics. They serve their faction through reconnaissance and swift strikes against enemies.'),
        ('Sand Ninja Jounin', 'An elite commander of Sand Ninja forces with years of combat experience. They lead squads on dangerous missions and train lower-ranking operatives.'),
        ('Sanda''s Noble Guard', 'A professional soldier sworn to protect Sanda and her interests. They maintain order and defend against threats with disciplined martial skill.'),
        ('Scavenger', 'A wasteland survivor who picks through ruins and battlefields for salvageable goods. They trade scrap and equipment to make a meager living.'),
        ('Scrawny Cannibal', 'A malnourished member of a cannibal tribe struggling to survive in harsh lands. Desperation has driven them to hunt other humans for sustenance.'),
        ('Screamer Unit', 'A specialized soldier equipped with sonic weaponry designed to disorient enemies. They operate in coordinated groups to maximize their tactical advantage.'),
        ('Shek Adventurer', 'A wandering Shek seeking glory and worthy opponents across the wasteland. They travel between towns taking contracts and testing their strength.'),
        ('Shek Barman', 'A Shek who serves drinks and manages a tavern establishment. They maintain order in their bar with intimidating presence and occasional force.'),
        ('Shek Engineer', 'A technically-minded Shek who maintains equipment and constructs defenses. They apply their strength and intellect to building and repair work.'),
        ('Shek Fighter', 'A combat-trained Shek warrior proficient in melee weapons and brawling. They seek honorable battles and respect strength above all else.'),
        ('Shek Medic', 'A Shek trained in battlefield medicine and emergency treatment. They patch up wounded warriors so they can return to honorable combat.'),
        ('Shek Recruit', 'A young Shek beginning their martial training and warrior education. They perform basic duties while learning combat skills from veterans.'),
        ('Shek Retainer', 'A loyal Shek warrior bound in service to a specific leader or household. They provide personal protection and carry out their master''s orders.'),
        ('Shek Scout', 'A fast-moving Shek who surveys terrain and tracks enemy movements. They report intelligence back to their commanders before battles.'),
        ('Shek Warrior', 'A seasoned Shek combatant hardened by numerous battles and conflicts. They embody their race''s martial culture and hunger for worthy challenges.'),
        ('Shinobi Citizen', 'A civilian resident of Shinobi Thieves territory living under their protection. They pay tribute and follow the faction''s laws in exchange for security.'),
        ('Shinobi Guard', 'An armed enforcer who patrols Shinobi Thieves settlements and territory. They protect faction interests and ensure tribute is properly collected.'),
        ('Shinobi Trader', 'A merchant operating under Shinobi Thieves oversight and protection. They buy and sell goods while paying their share to the faction.'),
        ('Shop Guard', 'A hired security professional who protects a store from thieves and troublemakers. They stand watch during business hours and deter potential criminals.'),
        ('Shrieking Bandit', 'A wild raider known for screaming battle cries during attacks. They terrorize travelers and small settlements for plunder and supplies.'),
        ('Skeleton Adventurer', 'An ancient skeleton exploring the world and seeking purpose in the current age. They wander between settlements offering their ageless experience for hire.'),
        ('Skeleton Bandit', 'A skeleton outlaw who preys on travelers and caravans for profit. Their mechanical body requires no food, only repair materials and equipment.'),
        ('Skeleton Barman', 'A skeleton who operates a drinking establishment serving organic customers. They never tire and have accumulated centuries of bartending knowledge.'),
        ('Skeleton Civilian', 'A skeleton living peacefully among other races in settled areas. They work various trades, unburdened by hunger or aging.'),
        ('Skeleton Doctor', 'A skeleton physician with extensive medical knowledge from past ages. They treat patients with techniques refined over centuries of practice.'),
        ('Skeleton Drifter', 'A wandering skeleton with no fixed home or allegiance, surviving through odd jobs and scavenging. They drift between settlements seeking purpose or simply avoiding trouble.'),
        ('Skeleton Grayflayer', 'An ancient skeleton warrior who has survived countless battles and wars. Their experience makes them formidable combatants despite their weathered frames.'),
        ('Skeleton Recruit', 'A newly activated or recently freed skeleton learning the ways of their current faction. They possess basic combat training but lack the experience of older models.'),
        ('Skeleton Resident', 'A skeleton who has settled permanently in a town or outpost, contributing to the community through labor or trade. They have found stability after potentially centuries of wandering.'),
        ('Skin Bandit', 'A deranged individual obsessed with collecting and wearing the skin of victims. They operate in gangs that hunt travelers across the wastes.'),
        ('Slave', 'A person stripped of freedom and forced into labor through capture or debt. They endure harsh conditions under constant guard and threat of punishment.'),
        ('Slave Escapee', 'Someone who has recently broken free from bondage and now flees their former masters. They carry the scars and trauma of enslavement while seeking a new life.'),
        ('Slave Hunter', 'A tracker specialized in recapturing escaped slaves for bounties. They employ nets, clubs, and tracking skills to return runaways to their owners.'),
        ('Slave Recruits', 'Newly captured individuals being processed into slavery, not yet broken or assigned permanent duties. They represent fresh acquisitions for the slave trade.'),
        ('Slave/Civilian', 'An enslaved person forced to perform domestic or urban labor within settlements. They serve households, shops, or public works under watchful supervision.'),
        ('Slave/Outlaw', 'A criminal sentenced to penal slavery as punishment for their crimes. They work in the harshest conditions as both punishment and deterrent.'),
        ('Slave/Ronin', 'A former warrior or samurai reduced to slavery through defeat or capture. Their combat skills make them valuable but dangerous property.'),
        ('Slave/Tough', 'An enslaved laborer assigned to physically demanding work in mines, farms, or construction. Their strength is exploited until exhaustion or death.'),
        ('Slave/Warrior', 'A slave forced to fight for their master''s entertainment or military purposes. They battle in arenas or serve as expendable troops.'),
        ('Slavemonger', 'A merchant who specializes in buying and selling slaves as commodities. They operate markets and auctions where human lives are traded for profit.'),
        ('Slaver', 'An individual who captures, trades, or guards slaves as their primary occupation. They view people as property and profit from human suffering.'),
        ('Slaver Boss', 'A leader commanding a slaver operation or camp with multiple subordinates. They manage the business of enslavement and extraction of labor.'),
        ('Slaver Caravan Boss', 'The commander of a mobile slaving operation that travels between regions buying and selling captives. They coordinate guards and manage valuable human cargo.'),
        ('Slaver Caravan Guard', 'An armed escort protecting slave caravans from raiders and preventing escape attempts during transport. They maintain order through intimidation and violence.'),
        ('Slaver Guard', 'A watchman stationed at slave camps or markets to prevent escapes and suppress resistance. They enforce discipline through brutality and constant surveillance.'),
        ('Slaver Heavy Guard', 'Elite enforcers equipped with superior armor and weapons to handle dangerous slaves or threats. They serve as the backbone of major slaving operations.'),
        ('Smuggler', 'A trader who moves contraband goods across faction borders, avoiding taxes and legal restrictions. They know secret routes and bribe the right officials.'),
        ('Sniperbot', 'An automated security unit programmed for long-range precision elimination of targets. It maintains watch over restricted zones with lethal accuracy.'),
        ('Soldier Drone', 'A basic military robot following simple combat protocols and orders. It serves as expendable infantry in automated defense forces.'),
        ('Soldierbot', 'An advanced combat automaton designed for frontline warfare and security operations. It executes tactical commands with mechanical efficiency and durability.'),
        ('Soldierbot Guard', 'An automated skeleton warrior programmed to defend a specific location or master. Its combat protocols are ancient but still deadly efficient.'),
        ('Starving Vagrant', 'A desperate wanderer on the edge of starvation, surviving day to day through begging or scavenging. They have nothing left to lose and everything to gain.'),
        ('Stormthrall', 'A warrior enslaved or indoctrinated to serve in the most brutal combat roles. They fight without question, broken by their masters or the wasteland itself.'),
        ('Straw Lieutenant', 'A mid-ranking officer in a local militia or bandit group, commanding small squads. They enforce orders and maintain discipline among the lower ranks.'),
        ('Strayed Paladin', 'A former Holy Nation warrior who abandoned or was exiled from their order. They wander seeking redemption or a new purpose beyond their failed faith.'),
        ('Surgeon', 'A skilled medical practitioner who repairs broken bodies in exchange for cats. Their services are expensive but essential in a world of constant violence.'),
        ('Swamp Ninja Chunin', 'A mid-level operative of the Swamp Ninjas, trained in stealth and assassination. They lead small teams on raids and intelligence gathering missions.'),
        ('Swamp Ninja Genin', 'A junior member of the Swamp Ninjas still learning the arts of infiltration and combat. They handle basic reconnaissance and support roles for the organization.'),
        ('Swamp Ninja Jonin', 'An elite Swamp Ninja commander with mastery over stealth warfare and tactical operations. They plan and execute the most critical missions for their faction.'),
        ('Swamper Bar Thug', 'A rough enforcer who keeps order in swamp town drinking establishments. They settle disputes with fists and blades when customers get too rowdy.'),
        ('Swamper Casino Dealer', 'A card and dice handler in the gambling dens of swamp settlements. They run games with practiced skill while watching for cheaters and troublemakers.'),
        ('Swamper Gate Guard', 'A sentry posted at the entrances to swamp settlements, checking travelers and collecting tolls. They turn away unwanted visitors and sound alarms during attacks.'),
        ('Swamper Non-Gang', 'An ordinary resident of the swamp towns trying to survive outside gang affiliations. They work honest jobs while avoiding the attention of local criminals.'),
        ('Sword For Hire', 'A mercenary warrior who sells their blade to whoever pays the most cats. They have no loyalty beyond the contract and move on when the job is done.'),
        ('Tech Hunter', 'A scavenger and explorer who seeks Ancient technology in ruins across the wasteland. They sell their findings to researchers or keep useful artifacts for themselves.'),
        ('Tech Hunter Adventurer', 'An experienced Tech Hunter who ventures into the most dangerous ruins for rare artifacts. They combine combat skills with knowledge of Ancient sites.'),
        ('Tech Hunter Gate Guard', 'A sentry protecting Tech Hunter outposts and camps from intruders. They screen visitors and defend valuable artifact collections stored within.'),
        ('Tech Hunter Guard', 'A warrior employed to protect Tech Hunter expeditions and facilities. They fight off bandits and creatures while salvage operations are underway.'),
        ('Tech Hunter Recruit', 'A novice member of the Tech Hunters learning to identify and extract Ancient technology. They assist veterans on expeditions while developing survival skills.'),
        ('Tech Hunter Ruins', 'A specialized scavenger operating deep within dangerous Ancient complexes. They navigate deadly security systems and hostile robots to claim lost technology.'),
        ('Tech Hunter Shopkeeper', 'A merchant who buys and sells Ancient artifacts and engineering equipment. They appraise technology and connect scavengers with wealthy collectors.'),
        ('Tenacious Recruit', 'A determined new fighter who refuses to give up despite lacking experience. Their persistence compensates for their current lack of skill and equipment.'),
        ('Territorial Thug', 'A violent enforcer who claims certain areas as their gang''s domain. They shake down travelers and merchants who pass through their controlled territory.'),
        ('Thief', 'A skilled pickpocket and burglar who steals to survive in the harsh world. They operate in shadows, taking what they need from the careless and wealthy.'),
        ('Thief Boss', 'The leader of an organized theft operation controlling multiple pickpockets and burglars. They plan heists and fence stolen goods through underground networks.'),
        ('Thief Fence', 'A shadowy merchant who buys stolen goods without asking questions. They operate from hidden locations and pay a fraction of market value for hot merchandise.'),
        ('Thrall', 'A broken slave who has endured years of brutal servitude in the Holy Nation. They perform backbreaking labor in fields and mines with little hope of freedom.'),
        ('Trade Goods Shopkeeper', 'A merchant specializing in raw materials and crafting supplies for travelers and craftsmen. They stock everything from iron plates to fabrics at fair prices.'),
        ('Traders Guard', 'A hired sword protecting merchant caravans as they cross dangerous territories. They must stay alert for bandits, beasts, and worse on the long roads.'),
        ('Traitorous Bar Thug', 'A disloyal enforcer willing to sell out their own gang for the right price. They lurk in taverns waiting for opportunities to betray their companions.'),
        ('Twitchy Bar Thug', 'A paranoid criminal whose nerves are shot from too many close calls and bad dust. They start fights over imagined slights and can barely hold a drink steady.'),
        ('UC Armour Trader', 'An official merchant licensed by the United Cities to sell protective gear. They offer quality armor at premium prices within UC territories.'),
        ('UC Citizen', 'A law-abiding resident of the United Cities who pays their taxes and follows the rules. They work honest jobs and avoid trouble with the Samurai enforcers.'),
        ('UC Hat Vendor', 'A specialized trader dealing exclusively in headwear from practical helmets to decorative hats. They maintain a small stall in UC marketplaces.'),
        ('UC Weapon Trader', 'A licensed arms dealer operating under United Cities authority. They sell quality blades and weapons to those who can afford the steep prices.'),
        ('Ugly Bar Thug', 'A scarred and brutish criminal whose appearance alone intimidates most patrons. They enforce protection rackets and collect debts through violence.'),
        ('Undertaker', 'A grim professional who handles corpse disposal in towns and cities. They collect bodies from the streets and prepare them for whatever burial customs apply.'),
        ('Unfortunate Recruit', 'A desperate soul who joined a faction out of necessity rather than conviction. They lack training and experience, making them cannon fodder in conflicts.'),
        ('Unique Recruits', 'Exceptional individuals with distinctive skills or backgrounds waiting to be discovered. Each has their own story and reason for joining a wandering group.'),
        ('United Hero', 'A celebrated warrior who has earned fame fighting for the United Cities. They command respect and higher pay for their proven combat abilities.'),
        ('Upgraded Skeleton Bandit', 'An ancient machine outlaw enhanced with superior components and weapons. They prey on travelers with mechanical efficiency and no mercy.'),
        ('Upgraded Skeleton Guard', 'A mechanical sentinel fitted with advanced armor plating and combat protocols. They protect important locations with tireless vigilance.'),
        ('Upgraded Watchbot', 'An enhanced security automaton patrolling settlements with improved sensors. They detect criminals and intruders more effectively than standard models.'),
        ('Vigilante Chief', 'A self-appointed leader of citizens who enforce their own justice outside the law. They organize patrols and punishments against those they deem criminals.'),
        ('Wall Man', 'A guard stationed on settlement walls watching for approaching threats. They spend long shifts scanning the horizon for bandits, beasts, or hostile forces.'),
        ('Wandering Assassin', 'A professional killer who travels between cities seeking contracts. They work for anyone who can meet their price, no questions asked.'),
        ('Waystation Barman', 'A tavern keeper running a remote establishment along major trade routes. They serve drinks and food to weary travelers while hearing all the latest rumors.'),
        ('Weak Thrall', 'A newly enslaved person not yet broken by the brutality of servitude. They still possess some spirit but lack the strength to resist their masters.'),
        ('White Eyebrow Grunt', 'A low-ranking member of the White Eyebrow bandit gang. They follow orders and participate in raids across the northern territories.'),
        ('Yabuta Outlaw', 'A criminal operating in the Yabuta region, preying on isolated farms and travelers. They survive through theft and violence in the harsh borderlands.')
), normalized AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT TRIM(name) AS name, TRIM(description) AS description
    FROM source_rows
    WHERE TRIM(name) <> '' AND TRIM(description) <> ''
)
INSERT INTO bio_random (type, description, name, race, gender, faction)
SELECT 'occupation', n.description, n.name, '', '', ''
FROM normalized n
ON CONFLICT (type, description, name) DO UPDATE
SET updated_at = NOW();
COMMIT;
